    <UnitTestResult executionId="ca24a2b7-54c6-4206-b602-58b208c0613a" testId="abe4d2cc-3ab1-da7c-cd2f-51496346b7e4" testName="Info_ResolvesDeployedDocumentationAndExamplesExecute(&quot;HASH-SHA3-256&quot;,32)" computerName="HOMEDEVICE" duration="00:00:00.0005570" startTime="2026-10-18T17:13:56.4401941+02:00" endTime="2026-10-18T17:13:56.4407514+02:00" testType="13cdc9d9-ddb5-4fa4-a97d-d965ccfc6d4b" outcome="Passed" testListId="8c84fa94-04c1-424b-9868-57a2d4851a1d" relativeResultsDirectory="ca24a2b7-54c6-4206-b602-58b208c0613a">
      <Output>
        <StdOut># MECHANISM HASH-SHA3-256&#xD;
&#xD;
HASH-SHA3-256 calculates an unkeyed message digest using the SHA3-256 hash function. It supports hashing rather than message authentication, encryption or decryption.&#xD;
&#xD;
---&#xD;
&#xD;
## Key Features&#xD;
&#xD;
- **Hash Function**: SHA3-256 belongs to the SHA-3 family, produces a 256-bit digest and is specified in FIPS 202.&#xD;
- **Input Data**: Hash accepts hexadecimal data, Base64 data, UTF-8 string data, or data stored in a VAR. Empty input is accepted.&#xD;
- **Digest Length**: Hash always returns the complete 32-byte SHA3-256 digest. The output length is not configurable.&#xD;
- **Return Value**: Hash returns a VAR containing hexadecimal digest bytes in 0x(...) format.&#xD;
- **Keys**: HASH-SHA3-256 is unkeyed. GenerateKey is not supported.&#xD;
&#xD;
## Functions&#xD;
The following functions are available for HASH-SHA3-256 mechanism:&#xD;
&#xD;
| Functions | Parameters | Input | Output | Key Length |&#xD;
|------------|-------------------|-------------------------------------|----------------|------------------|&#xD;
| Parameters | N/A | #MECH | PARAM variable | N/A |&#xD;
| Hash | #MECH | parameters, data | VAR digest | N/A |&#xD;
&#xD;
## Parameters&#xD;
These parameters are used with the HASH-SHA3-256 mechanism:&#xD;
- **#MECH**: Specifies HASH-SHA3-256 in PARAM.&#xD;
- **Additional Parameters**: Parameters rejects additional parameters.&#xD;
- **#IV**: Not supported.&#xD;
- **#PAD**: Not supported.&#xD;
- **#MACLEN**: Not supported.&#xD;
- **Salt and Output Length**: Not supported. The result always contains the complete 32-byte digest.&#xD;
&#xD;
---&#xD;
## Example Usage&#xD;
### HASH-SHA3-256 Digest Calculation&#xD;
PARAM p0       = Parameters(HASH-SHA3-256)  &#xD;
VAR cleartext  = "This is a secret message."  &#xD;
VAR digest     = Hash(p0, cleartext)  &#xD;
### HASH-SHA3-256 Empty Input&#xD;
VAR emptyhash  = Hash(p0, "")  &#xD;
&#xD;
---</StdOut>
      </Output>
    </UnitTestResult>
